##Summary

Linear search and binary search are two common searching techniques. Linear search checks elements one by one and can be used on both sorted and unsorted data. Its worst-case time complexity is O(n). Binary search works only on sorted data and repeatedly divides the search space into two halves

##Conclusion

The implementation and time analysis show that Binary Search is more efficient than Linear Search for large datasets, provided that the data is sorted. Linear Search is easier to implement and is suitable for small or unsorted datasets. Binary Search requires sorted data but significantly reduces the number of comparisons by dividing the search space into halves.
